#### BFF-to-Backend Service Communication

BFFs interact with backend microservices using standard patterns:

1. **Parallel Aggregation**: BFF makes concurrent calls to multiple backend services, aggregates responses
   ```javascript
   // Example: Mobile BFF aggregating member dashboard
   const [eligibility, claims, providers, benefits] = await Promise.all([
     memberService.getEligibility(memberId),
     claimsService.getRecentClaims(memberId),
     providerService.getProviders(memberProviderIds),
     benefitsService.getBenefits(memberId)
   ]);

   return aggregateForMobileDashboard({eligibility, claims, providers, benefits});
   ```

2. **Sequential Orchestration**: When backend calls depend on prior results
   ```javascript
   // Example: Partner BFF processing eligibility check
   const member = await memberService.findByMemberId(memberId);
   const coverage = await coverageService.getCoverage(member.planId, serviceDate);
   const authorization = await authService.checkAuthorization(coverage, procedureCode);

   return formatForPartnerResponse({member, coverage, authorization});
   ```

3. **Batch Optimization**: BFF batches multiple similar requests into single backend call
   ```javascript
   // Example: Web BFF loading claims list with provider names
   const claims = await claimsService.getClaims(filters);
   const providerIds = claims.map(c => c.providerId);
   const providers = await providerService.bulkGetProviders(providerIds); // Single call

   return claims.map(claim => ({
     ...claim,
     providerName: providers[claim.providerId].name
   }));
   ```

